From 2c3cc3037e51beca223de6ce2322b655719e9a99 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mqsirrel <68720462+Mqsirrel@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 23:01:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(settings): gate derive guidance behind an opt-in switch

Make CYB0X-S match its passive promise by default: nothing is derived on
import unless the operator opts in.

- Add src/cyb0x_s/settings.py with derive_guidance_enabled() / set_derive_guidance()
  / describe_derive_guidance(), reading CYB0X_DERIVE_GUIDANCE (off by default)
  and a session override for the TUI toggle.
- Gate derive_potential_and_next() so it returns ('', '') when disabled,
  leaving access_potential and next_action blank on imported services.
- Default access_potential to '' in the model, schema and store (was 'MED'),
  and update the upsert logic to keep an existing rating unless overridden.
- Wire a 'G' binding + action_toggle_derive_guidance() in the TUI.
- Update parser tests for the gated default and add tests/test_settings.py.

Co-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
